+### Mesh Initialization via QEM Decimation
+Takes a coarse geometric prior, such as a mesh decimated from a MobileNeRF output using QEM [S2, unofficial]. Initializes the DiffSoup optimization with this decimated mesh [S2, unofficial]. Iteratively prunes transparent primitives during optimization to obtain a clean triangle soup [S2, unofficial]. Training time with QEM initialization averages 8 minutes and 40 seconds [S2, unofficial]. Using QEM initialization achieves comparable reconstruction fidelity with a drastically reduced triangle count and significantly less time than retraining MobileNeRF (which takes over 6 hours) [S2, unofficial].
 
